    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>It's not about a career change or a different environment. It's like... the core architecture is just wrong. Every time I try to reboot or run a repair, the same fatal errors just pop up. I'm stuck in this infinite loop of failing processes. It feels like the only way to stop the logs from filling up with these useless error messages is to just stop the whole process. There's no point in trying to fix something that's designed to fail.",
